###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Water energy errors are in meV per H2O molecule (no schema unit; recorded with unit null). The paper states two DP rc = 6 A surface-training values (1.2 and 1.26 meV/H2O) and two test values (2.0 and 2.14 meV/H2O) in different passages; both are kept as written. The NaCl training accuracy (DP 7.6e-4 eV/atom and 2.0e-3 eV/A; DPLR 7.7e-4 eV/atom and 2.6e-3 eV/A) does not name the metric, so it is not encoded.
# - DW model centroid errors (1.7e-3 A training, 1.9e-3 A test) are not energy/force errors. The beta scan (Fig. 4) is figure-only. Dimer energies, free-energy profiles and NaCl phonons are properties.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/zhang2022.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

